nodecode-habitude is a rewrite of legott-ai's legott-ai/habitude-agent-integrations:

  https://github.com/legott-ai/habitude-agent-integrations
  commit 5802d0c9680f93a56440439bbfba189c80f1ec3f
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Habitude (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the four read-only Vault tools the plugin gave a model --
search_journal, read_excerpt, index_status and refresh_index -- and the scope
they ran in, one Markdown folder the user names. In the plugin those tools
were a Python MCP server the skill's setup reference started, with an SQLite
FTS5 cache, a small JSON config file and a Korean character-ngram tokenizer.
This cell declares the same four tools in Nodecode's own contract, walks the
folder's .md files itself, keeps the index in memory for the running process,
reads the vault folder from its own config section, and issues the same kind
of expiring reference so a citation is still checked against the note it came
from. Nothing is installed, nothing is executed, and no note is written.

Left out: the MCP stdio launcher and its JSON-RPC server (a cell registers
its tools in-process, so there is no server to start or handshake), the SQLite
FTS5 index (this one is rebuilt in memory, bounded by refresh_seconds), the
Korean character-ngram tokenizer and the journal-versus-derived-document
heuristics that ranked daily entries above generated reports -- matching here
is plainer word overlap over every note in the folder -- the skill's prose
procedure (the same guidance is the manual at (help :habitude)), the setup
helper that copied files into a harness skills directory, and the plugin's
other-harness packaging, which was not part of the hermes folder.
